[$in title:["Aliases"]]
[$in description:["Type aliases, dependency aliases and choice payload capture aliases in Moth."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
[section, $md:
    # Aliases

    An alias gives an existing type, dependency or payload field a local name. It
    doesn't create a value, conversion or new nominal type.

    Moth keeps `as` narrower than languages with broad renaming or casting
    syntax. The surrounding declaration always determines what gets renamed.
]

